# README for LlamaStack RAG Commands

These Python scripts interact with a LlamaStack deployment for document ingestion and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) chat.

---

## 1. Ingest Documents

Command to upload documents into the vector database for RAG:
`python ingest_docs.py [folder] [--base_url BASE_URL] [--vector_db_id VECTOR_DB_ID]`

- **`folder`** (required): Path to folder containing knowledge files to ingest (e.g., `./cost-data`).
- **`--base_url`**: Llama Stack base URL (default: `http://localhost:8321`).
- **`--vector_db_id`**: Optional existing vector database ID to reuse.  
  If not provided during ingestion, the system will look for the latest available vector database and ingest documents into it.  
  If no vector database exists, a new one will be created automatically.  

---

## 2. Chat with RAG

Command to chat interactively or using a questions file against the ingested knowledge base:
`python chat_with_rag.py [--base_url BASE_URL] [--tavily_api_key TAVILY_API_KEY] [--vector_db_id VECTOR_DB_ID] [--questions_file QUESTIONS_FILE]`

- **`--base_url`**: Llama Stack base URL (default: `http://localhost:8321`).
- **`--tavily_api_key`**: Tavily API key (required if using Tavily enhanced search).
- **`--vector_db_id`**: Optional vector database ID to specify which vector DB to query. If omitted, the system queries the latest available vector database by default.
- **`--questions_file`**: Optional file containing questions (one per line) to feed into the system.

Below are the questions_file available to try:
questions_idle_containers.json: Contains a list of questions designed to identify which containers have CPU usage idle.
questions_cost_optimization_v1.json, questions_cost_optimization_v2.json: Contain lists of questions tailored to discover cost optimization strategies based on trends observed in the data.

## 3. Create a New Vector Database [ to customize ]

Use the following script to create a new vector database in your LlamaStack deployment. This is useful to start a fresh vector DB with an automatically assigned unique ID.
`python create_vector_db.py --base_url <BASE_URL>`
- **`--base_url`**: Llama Stack base URL (default: `http://localhost:8321`).

---






